---
const indexEntries = [
  { customer: 'C2', order: 'O21' },
  { customer: 'C4', order: 'O12' },
  { customer: 'C4', order: 'O13' },
  { customer: 'C8', order: 'O22' },
  { customer: 'C9', order: 'O23' },
];
const orders = [
  { order: 'O12', customer: 'C4', total: '€36' },
  { order: 'O13', customer: 'C4', total: '€44' },
  { order: 'O22', customer: 'C8', total: '€24' },
  { order: 'O21', customer: 'C2', total: '€18' },
  { order: 'O23', customer: 'C9', total: '€40' },
];
---
<figure id="index-lookup" class="index-lookup paper-surface" aria-labelledby="index-lookup-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration</span>
  <h3 id="index-lookup-title">Find C4’s orders and their totals</h3>
  <p class="lookup-introduction">A scan checks the customer ID on every order. An index gives the engine another route: find C4 in the index, then locate its orders to read their totals.</p>
  <div class="lookup-drawing">
    <div class="lookup-part">
      <h4>Index on customer ID</h4>
      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">Index entries arranged by customer ID. The two entries for C4 locate orders O12 and O13.</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Customer ID</th><th scope="col">Locate order</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {indexEntries.map(entry => <tr class:list={{ match: entry.customer === 'C4' }}><th scope="row">{entry.customer}</th><td>{entry.order}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <svg class="lookup-paths" viewBox="0 0 70 336" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M 1 168 C 29 168, 39 120, 66 120" />
      <path d="M 59 115 L 66 120 L 59 125" />
      <path d="M 1 216 C 29 216, 39 168, 66 168" />
      <path d="M 59 163 L 66 168 L 59 173" />
    </svg>
    <div class="lookup-part">
      <h4>Orders table</h4>
      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">Five orders. Customer C4 has order O12 with a total of 36 euros and order O13 with a total of 44 euros.</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Order</th><th scope="col">Customer</th><th scope="col">Total</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {orders.map(order => <tr class:list={{ match: order.customer === 'C4' }}><th scope="row">{order.order}</th><td>{order.customer}</td><td>{order.total}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="lookup-answer"><strong>Answer: O12 (€36) and O13 (€44).</strong> C4 appears twice in this index because the customer has two orders. The index is extra information the database must maintain when orders change.</p>
  <figcaption>The totals are in the table, not this index. Order IDs label where the lookup leads; actual record locators depend on the engine. The drawing shows the route, not the work of searching the index.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .index-lookup { margin:2rem 0; padding:1.2rem; font:.875rem/1.6 var(--font-sans); }
  h3 { margin:0 0 .75rem; font:500 1.35rem/1.35 var(--font-serif); }
  .lookup-introduction { margin:0 0 1rem; font-size:.875rem; }
  .lookup-drawing { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 4.375rem minmax(0,1fr); align-items:start; }
  .lookup-part { min-width:0; }
  h4 { display:flex; align-items:center; height:3rem; margin:0; font:600 .875rem/1.4 var(--font-sans); }
  table { display:table; width:100%; margin:0; border-collapse:collapse; font:.875rem/1.4 var(--font-sans); }
  tr { height:3rem; }
  th,td { padding:0 .5rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); text-align:left; vertical-align:middle; }
  thead th { font-weight:500; font-size:.8125rem; }
  tbody th,tbody td { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-weight:400; }
  .match { background:var(--paper-match); }
  .match > :first-child { box-shadow:inset 3px 0 var(--teal); }
  .lookup-paths { display:block; width:100%; height:21rem; overflow:visible; color:var(--teal); }
  .lookup-paths path { fill:none; stroke:currentColor; stroke-width:1.5; stroke-linecap:round; stroke-linejoin:round; vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke; }
  .lookup-answer { margin:1.1rem 0 0; font-size:.875rem; }
  .lookup-answer strong { font-weight:600; }
  figcaption { border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); margin-top:1rem; padding-top:1rem; font-size:.8125rem; line-height:1.6; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  @media(max-width:560px) {
    .index-lookup { padding:.9rem; }
    .lookup-drawing { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:1rem; }
    .lookup-paths { display:none; }
    h4 { height:auto; min-height:2.5rem; }
    th,td { padding:0 .65rem; }
  }
</style>
